# Copy to .env.local and adjust.

# --- Database ---
# Local dev (docker compose up -d):
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://schoolcircle:schoolcircle@localhost:5432/schoolcircle?schema=public"
#
# Offline / edge (a Jetson at a schoolhouse) -- change the Prisma datasource provider to
# "sqlite" and use a file URL instead:
# DATABASE_URL="file:./schoolcircle.db"
#
# Enterprise (Track B) -- a managed Postgres in the approved enclave.

# --- Grounding engine (Anchor) ---
# The offline doctrine tutor. Unset = ungrounded fallback; set it to a running Anchor.
# DOCTRINE_BASE_URL="http://127.0.0.1:8000"
# DOCTRINE_TIMEOUT_MS="30000"

# --- Text model (generation) ---
# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint: a served open-weight LLM (the on-device gen model,
# vLLM, Ollama, TGI, ...). Self-hosted only -- the product is offline; no cloud API.
# Unset = generation features report 503 NO_PROVIDER (no mock or cloud fallback).
# BOTH MODEL_BASE_URL and MODEL_ID are required for the text capability to be ready.
# MODEL_BASE_URL="http://127.0.0.1:8001/v1"
# MODEL_ID="(your served model id)"
# MODEL_API_KEY=""   # only if your endpoint requires one

# --- Firebase Authentication (login) ---
# All PUBLIC client config (safe in the browser) -- from the Firebase console
# (Project settings -> Your apps -> Web app). Set these in Firebase App Hosting.
# If left unset, login is disabled and the app stays fully open (no lockout).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=""
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN="your-project.firebaseapp.com"
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID="your-project"
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET="your-project.appspot.com"
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=""
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=""

# --- Learning API (/api/learning, the Learn / Teach apps) ---
# Server-side identity: Firebase ID tokens are verified with the PUBLIC project id
# above (NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID). No service account is needed. Without
# it, /api/learning/* answers 401 and everything else stays open as before.
#
# Rubricon (rubric generation) and Whetstone (mastery sessions) call their own
# isolated OpenAI-compatible endpoints. Unset = those routes answer 503.
# RUBRICON_ENDPOINT="http://127.0.0.1:8001/v1/chat/completions"
# RUBRICON_MODEL="(your served model id)"
# RUBRICON_API_KEY=""
# WHETSTONE_ENDPOINT="http://127.0.0.1:8001/v1/chat/completions"
# WHETSTONE_MODEL="(your served model id)"
# WHETSTONE_API_KEY=""
#
# Run the Postgres-backed learning tests (npm test) against DATABASE_URL:
# RUN_DB_TESTS=1
